{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>In the best of the land settle your father.</b> For he is old and desires only rest and good air. But your brothers, young men — <b>let them dwell in the land of Goshen. A land</b> of pasture. And do not answer me from the etnaḥta, to say that it is a pausal break — for we find its parallel: ״זבולן עם חרף נפשו למות ונפתלי על מרומי שדה״." "<b>Men of ḥayil.</b> Expert in their craft, etc. — as in אשת חיל, which connotes wisdom. And one should not say it means what it sounds like literally, that it is not the way of women to go out to war or to army." "<b>And you shall appoint officers of livestock.</b> Over the horses, over the mules, and over the camels. And the proof is in Chronicles: ״ויקהל דוד את כל שרי ישראל ושרי כל רכוש ומקנה״ etc., and above it writes ״ועל הגמלים״. Another interpretation: since the flocks go in the wilderness to graze, in a place of predatory beasts and bandits, the shepherds need to be strong."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:55.264835814Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}